    "Solved Date": "2026-08-20 00:00:00",
    "Diagnostic": "• Julia asked what should move an order out of “In Fulfillment” (tracking number entered? pickup confirmed by reception?); the Fulfillment page will also get a filter to hide historical/closed orders by default. Axel proposed order_items.quantity_open = 0 as the “closed” signal (all items on an order must be closed for the order to close). Per Julia's Aug 20 Slack update, there's a richer flow to fold in: Sarah creates shipping labels in Apparel Magic — Airtable should reflect that (“Shipping label created”), auto-display the tracking number once it exists, close automatically when a bride picks up her gown in an appointment, and add a manual “Shipped” checkbox as an explicit staff confirmation step for shipped orders. Needs scoping: whether the AM-sourced label/tracking status should drive the transition on its own, or just be informational alongside quantity_open and the manual checkbox.\n• when an alterations line item is present it should register as picked (in-studio), not shipped; also clarified payment rule (alterations appointment confirmed only if alterations were purchased, otherwise payment required first). The payment-rule half already shipped (derived Paid/Unpaid column based on “Alterations” in Item Sold); the picked-vs-shipped fulfillment-status semantic isn't yet confirmed fixed.",
