    "#": 29.0,
    "Short Name": "Pipeline — Order Ready, Alterations & Fulfillment Per-Order Fields (Unassigned)",
    "Full Description": "Several stage-view fields on Order Ready, Alterations, and Fulfillment are set at the bride level when they should be tracked per order, and stage columns aren't reflecting recently scheduled alterations appointments.",
    "Report Date": null,
    "Owner": "Singular",
    "Priority": "2. High",
    "Status": "Done",
    "Source": null,
    "Singular Dev": "Axel",
    "Solved Date": null,
    "Diagnostic": "• alterations appointments scheduled in the past 7 days aren't showing up in the Alterations column of the Pipeline Kanban — needs review against live Acuity data.\n• the Fulfillment column isn't showing any appointments from the last 7 days; the automation that should trigger this change appears not to have been updated — likely resolves alongside the Fulfillment & Alterations Logic work Axel owns.\n• Pick Up and Ship fields on Order Ready track whether the selected fulfillment method was completed, not which method was chosen — proposed fix is an inline Orders table showing each order's own fulfillment method, since a bride can have multiple orders with different methods.\n• the manual Client Notified checkbox on Order Ready should become a rollup (% of orders where the client has been notified), with an editable Client Notified field added to the same inline orders table.\n• on Alterations, the Last Alterations Appt timezone doesn't parse correctly, the Alterations Lead should display even when empty, and two new fields are proposed — an Alterations In House button for SAs (“No Alterations” / “Alterations Needed”) and an Alterations Status single-select (Pending by default, shown only when Alterations In House or Shopify Alteration Order is TRUE). This ties directly into the Order Ready → In Fulfillment stage rework: gown ready + no alterations → In Fulfillment; gown ready + alterations done → In Fulfillment; gown ready + alterations pending → stays Order Ready (or In Alterations if scheduled); Alterations Status feeds the Stage formula directly. Questions sent to Julia for confirmation Aug 20, pending her reply before build.\n• on In Fulfillment, Fulfillment Method, Client Notified, Tracking Number, and 3PL are per-order attributes displayed as if they were general to the bride — the same per-order fix direction as the Pick Up/Ship and Client Notified items above, using an inline table with those columns editable except 3PL; the hardcoded “Tax + Shipping” values should be removed once this lands, since they no longer apply.",
    "Solution": "Issue 1 — Alterations/Fulfillment columns weren't reflecting recent appointments\nFixed the sync bug (pointed at a deprecated appointment-type field). While rolling it out we found something bigger: stage was being written by 8 uncoordinated automations, which briefly moved a batch of clients backward — corrected everyone affected, and started a rework so stage gets computed from independent one-way facts instead of being overwritten directly, making this bug class structurally impossible going forward. Status: built and validated in Sandbox/Production; the final cutover is paused until Julia reviews the new logic.\n\nIssue 2 — Fulfillment column wasn't reflecting recent pickups\nFound the cause: the automation was reading a deprecated appointment-type field and was also missing a few valid pickup appointment types in its trigger. Fixed both, then backfilled every client who had already picked up but was stuck waiting. Status: live in Production.\n\nIssue 3 — Pick Up/Shipping on Order Ready tracked method, not completion\nRemoved the manual \"Shipping\"/\"Pick Up\" checkboxes (only worked for one order per bride) and replaced them with a table showing every one of her orders, each with its fulfillment method and a real progress bar for how much has been picked up/shipped. Status: live in Sandbox.\n\nIssue 4 — Client Notified was a manual checkbox\nIt's now a progress bar showing the % of a bride's orders where the client has actually been notified, calculated automatically instead of checked by hand. Status: live in Sandbox and Production.\n\nIssue 5 — Alterations: timezone, Alterations Lead, In House button, Alterations Status\nFixed a timezone bug in alterations appointment times (was showing the viewer's own timezone instead of the studio's). Alterations Lead now always shows. Alterations In House is now a clear button instead of a checkbox. Added a new Alterations Status field (starts at \"Pending\"), with its options and colors pulled live from Airtable. Status: live in Sandbox and Production; Julia's confirmation on the full status list still pending (two choices so far: \"Pending\", \"Done\").\n\nIssue 6 — Fulfillment Method/Client Notified/Tracking/3PL were bride-level, not per-order\nRemoved the bride-level Fulfillment Method, Client Notified, Tracking #, and 3PL fields on In Fulfillment and replaced them with a table showing every one of the bride's orders, each with its own method, notified status, tracking number, and 3PL, plus a real progress bar. Fulfillment Method and Client Notified are editable per order; Tracking # and 3PL stay read-only. Also fixed the underlying progress calculation, which was double-counting \"picked\" (ready to hand off) and \"shipped\" (already handed off) as if they were two halves of the same total. Status: live in Sandbox and Production.",
